    "title": "Clean-endpoint resultant boundary saturation",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "leading-coefficient Bezout and exact resultant degree",
    "statement": "At the clean endpoint, the domain complement has exact parameter degrees deg_z W=T and deg_z V=3m+1, with q_inf*nu+P_sat*omega=1. The top weld coefficient forces q_inf to divide the leading coefficient of B. In fact Res_z(Q,W)=c_W(X-x_0)^(m-1), Res_z(Q,B)=c_B q_inf^(T+deg_z B)(X-x_0), and resultant degree saturation forces deg_X B=N. Thus B absorbs the entire parameter-infinity fibre and the boundary-free shortcut is impossible.",
